WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.162
SMS Organizer was downloaded over a million times,

2
00:00:04.162 --> 00:00:07.554
and it sorted every message on the phone itself.

3
00:00:07.904 --> 00:00:12.481
People loved what it did. Reviews kept asking for an app that looked the part.

4
00:00:20.067 --> 00:00:21.349
My audit showed why.

5
00:00:21.699 --> 00:00:24.571
Two navigation bars competed for attention,

6
00:00:24.571 --> 00:00:26.975
text was small and low in contrast,

7
00:00:26.975 --> 00:00:29.068
reminders stopped at the alert,

8
00:00:29.068 --> 00:00:33.254
and some messages arrived in languages readers couldn't read.

9
00:00:35.367 --> 00:00:36.399
The app was smart.

10
00:00:36.749 --> 00:00:38.118
The interface didn't show it.

11
00:00:40.533 --> 00:00:43.583
First, I moved the main navigation to the bottom,

12
00:00:43.583 --> 00:00:47.630
within thumb reach, and turned the top bar into message filters.

13
00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:51.658
Larger text and stronger contrast cleared the rest of the noise,

14
00:00:51.658 --> 00:00:54.704
and the update asks people before it moves anything.

15
00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:58.666
Reminders used to stop at the alert.

16
00:00:59.016 --> 00:01:01.984
Now the app creates them from booking messages,

17
00:01:01.984 --> 00:01:03.310
groups them by type,

18
00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:07.351
and a tap opens the next step, like hotels at your destination.

19
00:01:09.567 --> 00:01:13.158
An SMS arrives in whatever language the sender chose.

20
00:01:13.508 --> 00:01:15.702
So people pick their language once,

21
00:01:15.702 --> 00:01:19.339
then translate any message into it or hear it read aloud,

22
00:01:19.339 --> 00:01:22.661
and every layout holds when a translation runs long.

23
00:01:24.867 --> 00:01:26.066
In UX Labs testing,

24
00:01:26.066 --> 00:01:30.107
people preferred the new design for its layout and modern look.

25
00:01:30.457 --> 00:01:35.649
It shipped on a Material 3 design system I built. Engagement rose 30%.

26
00:01:38.733 --> 00:01:43.587
Redesigning an app people already use is a migration as much as a launch.
